# Token optimization

## Rules budget
- Keep all `alwaysApply: true` rules under ~2,000 tokens combined.
- One concern per `.mdc` file. Use `globs` for file-type rules.
- Never paste style guides — use linters and link to `.cursor/reference/`.

## Chat hygiene
- **One task = one chat.** Long threads re-send history and degrade focus.
- Use `@Past Chats` to pull selective context into a fresh session.
- Revert and re-plan instead of debugging a confused multi-turn thread.

## Context selection
- `@file` when you know the answer lives there; `@folder` for structure; let the agent search when unsure.
- Attach 2–4 files max unless the task truly needs more.
- Disable unused MCP servers — their tool schemas load every Agent turn.

## LLM-as-wiki
- Compile knowledge once into `docs/wiki/index.md` + topic pages.
- On code changes, update only affected wiki pages (surgical diffs).
- See `.cursor/reference/llm-wiki-pattern.md` and the `wiki-maintain` skill.

## Audit checklist
1. Dashboard → Usage: identify expensive sessions.
2. Trim always-on rules and Memories.
3. Scope rules with globs; move workflows to Skills.
4. Use Auto/Composer for routine work; frontier models for plan/review only.
